@startuml services-evict-sequence
' How an eviction reaches the running server after MRD-247.
' Before the fix the admin tool's invalidate() removed a key that was never stored
' and, being a separate JVM, could not reach the server's cache at all.
title Cache eviction across two JVMs (MRD-247, after)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

box "Admin tool JVM (AdminCli evict GUELPH 2025)" #F4F4F4
  participant AdminCli
  participant "ForecastCache\n(admin's own)" as AC
  participant "EvictionMarks\n(admin's own)" as AM
end box

database "<store path>.evict/\nGUELPH" as Notes

box "Server JVM (ApiServer, :8081)" #F4F4F4
  participant ForecastV2
  participant "ForecastCache\n(server's)" as SC
  participant "EvictionMarks\n(server's)" as SM
end box

== Admin tool: evict ==
AdminCli -> AC : summary("GUELPH")  (warm-up)
AdminCli -> AC : invalidate("GUELPH", 2025)
AC -> AC : entries.remove(key("GUELPH"))
AC -> AM : mark("GUELPH")
AM -> Notes : write temp file, then atomic move\nnew random token
note right of AM
  Throws IOException if the note cannot be written.
  AdminCli reports that instead of claiming
  an eviction that did not reach the server.
end note

== Server: next /api/v2/forecast read ==
ForecastV2 -> SC : summary("GUELPH")
SC -> SM : token("GUELPH")
SM -> Notes : read
SM --> SC : token (NONE if no note, UNKNOWN on trouble)
alt entry cached AND younger than TTL AND token is known AND entry.token == token
  SC --> ForecastV2 : cached Summary
else otherwise (evicted, expired, or token unreadable)
  SC -> SC : load("GUELPH")  (SELECT COUNT, MAX, AVG ... via DbClient)
  opt token is not UNKNOWN
    SC -> SC : entries.put(key, Entry(fresh, now, token))
  end
  SC --> ForecastV2 : fresh Summary
end
@enduml
